.SH NAME
polaric-newcert \- Create certificate and certificate request
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B polaric-newcert
.br

.SH DESCRIPTION
This utility generates a self-signed certificate (with a key) and certficate signing request (CSR). The key and the certificate
is placed in /etc/polaric-webapp/ssl so that they can be used by the frontend Webserver. This command is run at first-time
installation but can also be used later to create a new key and certificate. If the callsign of the server is changed, it is 
strongly recommended to re-run this command so that the correct callsign is reflected in the certificate. 
The keypair is based on elliptic curves (P-256). 

If a signing service (CA) is available and the polaric-certauth-client is installed and correctly configured, the command 
polaric-signcert can be used to get a signed certificate (by using the CSR). 
.PP
